WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.730
- Recently someone asked me
what the most important element

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.560
of a business slide presentation is.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.977
And after thinking about it for a bit,

00:00:07.977 --> 00:00:09.900
it was very clear to me

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.070
that Action Titles are actually
the most important elements.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.950
So by now you're not really
sure what an Action Title is,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.830
or how to come up with a very,
very strong Action Title,

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.550
welcome come to another video here

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.490
on my channel "Firm Learning".

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.530
My name is Heinrich, I'm a
former McKinsey consultant,

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.620
and on my channel I
talk a lot about topics

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.240
such as career success,
and also consulting skills.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.690
And surely as a consultant,

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.030
one thing that you really need to do well,

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.670
is to create slide presentations,

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:42.130
in PowerPoint or any of
these other programs.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.190
So in today's video,

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.830
I want to sharpen your understanding

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.880
why Action Titles are so important,

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.690
and also give you some
very, very tangible tips,

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.560
including an exercise to help you come up

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.223
with the best possible Action Titles

00:00:54.223 --> 00:00:55.990
that you can write for your slides.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.110
Let's start by looking into

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.420
why Action Titles are so important.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.410
And the key point you're to understand,

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.920
is that your presentations
should have a storyline.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:09.030
And it is the Action Titles
that bring this story to life.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.270
The main idea is that

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.440
if you read your titles
of your presentation,

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.820
from start to end,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.160
so every single slide
just read the titles.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.010
The key idea is that by just doing that,

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:25.040
you will be able to understand
all the key messages

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.220
of the presentation just by
reading these Action Titles.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.760
So why is this even necessary?

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.040
Why is this important?

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.300
Well try to put yourself into the shoes

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.920
of a C level manager,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.770
you are a CEO, CFO, any
other business unit head,

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.060
any other senior guy in an organization.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.620
Likely especially these
large blue chip companies

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.120
that often these consulting
firms we work for,

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.880
these C level people,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.310
every single day, every single week,

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.900
they will get several big
documents, 50 pages, 100 pages,

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.930
or even more of other
projects that are going on.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:01.690
Project updates, progress
reports, deliverables like that.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.500
This is far too much to read.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.170
People like this cannot
just read every single slide

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.340
of documents like that.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.550
So what they will expect you
to deliver as a document,

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.500
where they can just skim through,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.020
just read the Action Titles,

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:19.400
and just by reading the Action Titles,

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.110
be able to understand
all the key messages.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:26.100
And this is the so-called
horizontal logic,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.320
the storyline of the presentation,

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.630
this needs to come to life,
via the Action Titles.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.130
And then the idea is of course,

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.916
that if they read something
in the Action Title,

00:02:34.916 --> 00:02:36.600
that is really interesting,

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.490
where they want to learn more about,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.150
then they stop, and
then they read the page,

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.470
they read the full slide.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.250
This then is the vertical logic.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.083
And you of course,

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:47.740
you already understand one key thing

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.650
when writing strong Action Titles.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.620
And this is that of
course an Action Title,

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.440
should summarize the contents of a slide

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.880
in a clear and concise way.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.080
So this is the intuition,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.230
but now you might ask yourself,

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:03.300
well, what exactly is an Action Title?

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.680
So I try to put down here in definition.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.200
This is coming from myself.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.650
So no fancy source,

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.570
just my best way of putting it in writing.

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.200
And I would define an Action Title

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.240
by being a header of a slide presentation,

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.710
that summarizes the content of the slide,

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.620
by formulating a complete sentence.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.550
So if you wanted something
like here, the header,

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.470
also here on top of this slide saying,

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.740
Action Titles have to
create your storyline

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.000
within a presentation.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.230
This would be the Action
Title of that slide.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.580
This is what you want to try to achieve.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.850
But what do you write in such a title?

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.610
What are the contents supposed to be?

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.990
And here I think the best
test that you can do,

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.440
is the test of the so called, so what?

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.290
The question of the, so what?

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.220
And a one screen of full video

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.170
just about the concept of
asking this question, so what?

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.570
I will link it somewhere above here

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:54.600
if you're interested to learn
more about this feel free

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.560
to check it out.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:56.840
But in a nutshell,

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.460
the so what is a question,

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.080
that you as a project lead,

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:03.040
might ask to an associate, a
consultant to prepare the slide

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.600
or maybe a partner asked to you.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.600
And this person looks at your slide,

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.170
and asks him or herself
the question, so what?

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.360
Right? So, so what?

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.960
Why is this irrelevant?

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.400
What is the implication
of what I see here?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.150
Because maybe the information
on the slide is interesting,

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.490
it's data, it's nice,

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.630
but what does this mean
for the problem at hand?

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.260
For the thing that I need to solve?

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.700
So when putting together the document,

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:29.960
you should ask yourself,

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:32.150
what is the so what on the slide?

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.490
If already you struggle to
come up with the so what,

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.310
then this often is a sign

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.540
that this slide maybe isn't
that important, right?

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.690
If it does not have a clear so what?

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:43.190
Maybe it's something that
rather belongs in the appendix

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:44.670
but maybe not in the main deck

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.430
or maybe take it out completely.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.590
But once you know the so what?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.840
Make sure that the so
what is clearly stated

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:50.900
in the Action Title,

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.570
and then of course, when
you are presenting the slide

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:56.370
then the so what is also what
you should be communicating

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.320
in your presentation.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.810
Now let's look into a
couple of best practices

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.570
that you should apply whenever
you write an Action Title.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.310
And here we'll always have an example,

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.940
and then an insight that I
wanna draw out from that.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.497
The first example is,

00:05:08.497 --> 00:05:13.230
"Managing risk is important
for this project's success".

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.180
And here my answer is, try to
avoid statements like that.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.560
Try to avoid writing general truths,

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.240
that are pretty much always correct.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.070
So of course, managing risks
is pretty much always important

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:26.550
for this project's success, right?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.570
So for almost every project
that would be relevant.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:32.010
So try to avoid writing
things that are obvious,

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:36.270
really draw out more
insightful things than that.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.620
Next, something like,
"All divisions have found

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:42.400
to not be following best practices".

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.780
What's often dangerous,
is to write Action Titles

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.750
with really hard absolute statements,

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:53.120
always never in every case,
this is like this or like that.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.640
So these very hard statements,

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.350
often are traps

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.220
because there are often
some weird edge cases.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.050
Maybe there is this, like very
little division somewhere,

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.120
who does something that
you are not aware of.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.710
Just my personal learning,

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.610
that often then especially
if you're presented,

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:11.270
maybe there is like one board
member sitting in the audience

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.230
who will tell you,

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:13.670
no, but this is not correct.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:14.530
This is wrong.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:17.500
'Cause you know, it's
just enough of one example

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:18.610
that contradicts this,

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.570
and then pretty much you're
there, need to admit that,

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.373
yes, your message was wrong,

00:06:22.373 --> 00:06:24.150
what you put on the slide was wrong.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.560
It's not the case, that this
is true for all divisions.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.477
Next one.

00:06:28.477 --> 00:06:33.120
"Company has potential to
significantly improve profit".

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.660
So here my learning from that is,

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.790
try to whenever possible to
quantify the Action Titles.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.060
Include numbers in the Action Titles.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.220
So if you make a slide
about profit of a company

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.570
usually you should always
be able to support a number.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:48.170
So what is the profit
improvement potential?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.910
What is the potential for the profit

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:51.330
that you see in the company?

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.163
Next one.

00:06:52.163 --> 00:06:54.367
"When conducting data
analysis and interviews,

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:56.980
"we learnt a lot about the business".

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:58.580
So this would be an Action Title

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.560
which very much focuses on the process.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:05.230
So what you did, you analyzed
data, conducted interviews,

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.160
you learned a lot.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.210
This is often not so relevant.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.270
People don't really
care to who you talk to,

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:12.070
what analysis you conducted,

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:15.430
what people are interested
in are the results.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.850
This is one of the key
fundamental principles

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.780
of top down communication.

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:22.540
Again, I don't wanna go too
deep into this in this video

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.230
but I will link another video that I did

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.630
about top down communication, about fear,

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:30.060
check it out, really one of
the most fundamental concepts

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:33.330
for communication as a
consultant but also in general,

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.640
in any professional environment.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:36.777
Last example here,

00:07:36.777 --> 00:07:39.087
"Results indicate significant potential

00:07:39.087 --> 00:07:42.137
"to look into further improvement
measures for the business

00:07:42.137 --> 00:07:45.007
"with the goal to increase profits by 50%

00:07:45.007 --> 00:07:48.750
"until end of this financial
year for the company".

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.050
So frankly I don't even know
what exactly this means.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:52.960
The point that I wanted to make here is,

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:55.940
write Action Titles in a concise way.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.410
Don't use more words than necessary.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.470
Yes, usually there will
be a full sentence,

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:04.150
but don't just write
for the sake of writing.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.300
The rule is that usually, in the title,

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:09.300
you should not have more
than two lines of titles.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.840
So two lines are fine, but
not right more than two.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.720
Now let's put your Action Title
writing abilities to test.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.870
You see here a standard slide,

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.370
it's from a mock up presentation.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.110
Of course not any actual line engagement,

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:24.590
but what you see here is a slide

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.470
where the Action Title is missing.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:30.130
And I want now you to come
up, with an Action Title.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.000
And now to help a little bit out here

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.880
we just like briefly
expand what you see here.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:37.370
So here you see a sizing
of a growth potential,

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.800
EBIT potential for this company

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.100
that could choose to enter these market.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:45.500
So the North America market,
or the Asia Pacific market,

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.680
and then you see different
numbers, you see the market size,

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.180
you see how much of the market
is covered by competitors,

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.630
the current market share,

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.360
and other considerations like this,

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.450
and in the end, also an EBIT potential,

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:00.600
that the company could receive
from entering these markets.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.680
Now I would encourage you

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.210
to maybe even pause
the video for a moment,

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.670
and think about for yourself,

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.910
what would be a strong Action Title,

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:09.500
for such a slide.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.330
If you want even write it down.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:12.960
So let's look at the couple of examples

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.570
of what you could have written.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:15.487
So the first is,

00:09:15.487 --> 00:09:18.270
"Derived potentials for an expansion".

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:19.920
And again, feel free to always pause

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.370
and think about this for yourself,

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.203
whether you consider

00:09:22.203 --> 00:09:24.480
that this is a strong Action Title or not.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.160
Because indeed I would argue,

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:27.910
this is not even an Action Title.

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:30.950
This does not even meet the
definition of an Action Title.

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:32.450
This is a title in the style

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.330
that I know many people like to do it,

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.350
but it's just not what I
would recommend you to do.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:37.480
And this is for instance

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:40.760
if you have a page that
describes the risks

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.580
of a certain strategy,

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:45.560
then just writing risks
in the title, right?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.140
So it's a title, but
it's not an Action Title

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:49.240
in the sense that,

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.120
it doesn't summarize the key message

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:54.720
of a slide in a full sentence.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:55.887
Next one.

00:09:55.887 --> 00:09:57.617
"Expand into new geographies

00:09:57.617 --> 00:10:00.730
"creates a positive EBIT potential".

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:03.230
EBIT by the way, for the
uninitiated stands for,

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:05.150
Earnings Before Interest and Tax,

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:07.710
and pretty much is one
metric of profit, right?

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:11.640
So what is the profit, the
profit potential of the company.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:13.490
So what do you think
about this Action Title?

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:16.980
And to you I would argue that
yes, it meets the definition.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:19.430
I mean, it is an Action Title
following the definition,

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.193
but I would argue it's
not the best Action Title

00:10:21.193 --> 00:10:22.570
that you could write.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:25.970
Because indeed this seems far too generic.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:28.540
You could be much more tangible,
much more concrete here.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:30.557
But let's look into a
couple of other examples.

00:10:30.557 --> 00:10:33.217
"Expansion to North
America and Asia Pacific,

00:10:33.217 --> 00:10:36.040
"creates a positive EBIT potential".

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:36.920
I mean, yes, I like it.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:39.040
It's a bit more rich of information.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.640
You're not just talking about geographies

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.490
but are really mentioning
geographies you're interested in

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:45.800
but, here quantify if possible.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.970
We just looked at these best practices.

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:48.930
Whenever possible,

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.920
especially whenever you
have numbers available

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.090
at your disposal,

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:54.820
put them in the Action
Title and quantify it.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:55.653
Next one.

00:10:55.653 --> 00:10:57.397
"Expansion to North
America and Asia Pacific

00:10:57.397 --> 00:11:01.970
"creates a positive EBIT
potential of 22 Euro million".

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.410
So yes, here I would argue,

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:05.300
it's fine, it's already a very strong

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:06.720
and solid Action Title,

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.583
though here you could argue

00:11:07.583 --> 00:11:09.810
that this is still a little bit too wordy.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:13.180
You could write this in
a bit more concise way.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:16.380
Usually, the fewer words
you use, the better.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.647
So here one example,

00:11:17.647 --> 00:11:19.937
"Expansion to North
America and Asia Pacific

00:11:19.937 --> 00:11:22.920
"with 22 Euro million EBIT potential".

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:23.753
And I would argue that,

00:11:23.753 --> 00:11:26.300
yes, this is a good
and solid Action Title.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:27.690
You know, what's also
important to understand,

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:29.430
is then you wanna write
these Action Titles,

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.770
you do not need to write
them like you would write

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:34.620
like proper full sentences in a book.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.790
It's completely fine to
take out certain words,

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:40.670
often you take out articles,
any other filler words,

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.710
which are not absolutely necessary

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.160
to understand the key messages.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:46.200
Obviously you would probably
not write something like this

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.520
as a full sentence in a book.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:51.770
But here's a concise Action
Title, this is absolutely fine.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.310
So hope this makes sense to you.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.150
